# Line-ending policy.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the development machine, so without a rule here Git
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For ordinary sources that is harmless. For
# HASH-LOCKED EVIDENCE it is not: the recorded sha256 is the integrity control
# that proves a human score was not edited after unblinding, and a line-ending
# conversion would silently change every byte-level check that depends on it.
#
# `-text` stores and restores these files verbatim, with no conversion in either
# direction.

# Gate-1 and Gate-2 human scoring artifacts, verified by sha256 in pytest.
docs/evidence/prototype-4/pilot-scoring-form-completed-blind.md -text

# Frozen manifests and recorded run evidence are hashed by the tooling.
data/manifests/*.csv -text
docs/evidence/**/*.jsonl -text
